:PNLGRP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME=SQL.SQL Query Manager
:P.This command was created to allow working with SQL queries. The program
provides means of saving queries, adding variables, emailing the results
and much more.
:P.The primary function of the command is to work with SELECT queries.
The initial command is SQL but there are several options to allow editing
or running a specific query.
:P.Enter the command SQL and press F4 to view the options. Press F1 for
examples and help with the command.
:H2.Example 1:
:P.Entering the query maintenance program.
:P.SQL <enter>
:H2.Example 2:
:P.Running an ad hoc query on a specific file.
:P.SQL INVENPF <enter> where INVENPF is the name of a physical file
:H2.Example 3:
:P.Emailing a saved query.
:P.SQL SAVEDQRY *EMAIL
:P.Where SAVEDQRY is a query already setup in the maintenance program.
:H2.Example 4:
:P.Emailing a passed query.
:P.SQL 'select * from custpf' *EMAIL
:P.In a CL program the query can be passed in a variable. Make sure
any quotation marks are doubled within the query string.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/FILE'.File/Query Name - HELP
:XH3.FILE - File/Query Name
:P.This field allows entry of either a file name or a query name.
If the action option is left the default of *ADHOC the program
expects this to be the name of a file. In this case the program
will load to the ad hoc query screen with a default query statement
of SELECT * FROM <FILENAME>.
:P.If the action option is changed to any other value, the program
will expect a query name to be entered here. The query name needs to
already be setup in the SQL Query Manager program.
:P.See the help text for the action field to learn more about how the
file field is used with each type of action.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/ACTION'.Action - Help
:XH3.ACTION - Action to take.
:P.This parameter lists allows entry of the action to take
when the program is run.  It defaults to *ADHOC which is a dual
purpose action. *ADHOC is ignored if no file name is passed so
so the program just loads to the main maintenance screen. The rest
of the values are list below.
be added after it.
:UL.
:LI.:HP2.*ADHOC:EHP2. - If a file name is passed opens the ad hoc query screen.
:LI.:HP2.*EDIT:EHP2. - Requires a query name in the FILE parameter, opens
the program straight to the update screen for that query.
:LI.:HP2.*PRINT:EHP2. - Requires a query name in the FILE parameter, runs
the query output to a spool file.
:LI.:HP2.*EMAIL:EHP2. - Requires a query name in the FILE parameter, emails
the query output as an attachment.
:LI.:HP2.*DISPLAY:EHP2. - Requires a query name in the FILE parameter,
displays the output from the query.
:LI.:HP2.*OUTFILE:EHP2. - Requires a query name in the FILE parameter,
creates a physical file containing the results of the query.
:LI.:HP2.*IFSFILE:EHP2. - Requires a query name in the FILE parameter,
creates a PC stream file with the result of the query.
:LI.:HP2.*VIEW:EHP2. - Requires a query name in the FILE parameter, opens
displays the queries definition.
:EUL.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/USER'.User that created the query (USER) - Help
:XH3.USER - User that created the query.
:P.Specifies the user that created the query. This is needed because
the system allows the same query name under different users. This means
to run a query that someone else created thier user profile name needs
to be passed to the program.
:NT.If the query is being run from a program that multiple people
will be using, the user should always be hard coded so the same query
is run regaurdless of who is signed on.:ENT.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/EMAIL'.Email Address - Help
:XH3.EMAIL - Email Addresses
:P.Specifies the email address to send to Excel file to. This option
is only displayed if the ACTION is *EMAIL.
:P.The field allows email addresses up to 50 characters and allows up
50 addresses to be included.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK def.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The email address stored in the ACCESSPF for the current
user running the job is used.
:PT.:PK.*RPTDSTID:EPK.
:PD.The RPTDSTID field is displayed and a report distribution ID
can be entered. The email addresses will be pulled from that ID.
:PT.:Pk.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default email address setup in the query deffinition will
be used.
:PT.:PV.email-address:EPV.
:PD.Specify the email address of the recipient.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/RPTDSTID'.Report Distribution ID (RPTDSTID)- Help
:XH3.RPTDSTID - Report Distribution ID
:P.Specifies a report distribution ID to pull the email addresses from.
:NT.This parameter will not be displayed unless a special value of
*RPTDSTID is entered in the email field.:ENT.
:P.The email addresses will be pulled from ACCESSPF for all users
setup in the report distribution queue for the EMAIL/*ALL/*ALL
entry.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/FILENAME'.File Name (FILENAME)- Help
:XH3.FILENAME - File Name
:P.Specifies the name of the file attached to the email. Do not include
the file extension, it will be added automatically based on the file
type parameter.
:P.This option is only displayed if the ACTION is *EMAIL.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/TYPE'.File Type (TYPE)- Help
:XH3.TYPE - File Type
:P.Specifies the type of file to contain the queries output.
The valid type are:
:UL.
:LI.:HP2.*XLS:EHP2. - Creates an Excel file.
:LI.:HP2.*XML:EHP2. - Creates an Excel formatted XML file.
:LI.:HP2.*CSV:EHP2. - Creates a Comma Separated Variable text file.
:EUL.
:P.This option is only displayed if the ACTION is *EMAIL.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/SUBJECT'.Subject (SUBJECT) - Help
:XH3.SUBJECT - Subject
:P.Specifies the subject for the email. CHAR(128)
:NT.When prompting, the input field can be expanded
by entering an ampersand (&) in the first position of
the field, followed by a blank.:ENT.
:P.This option is only displayed if the ACTION is *EMAIL.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK def.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.No subject is included in the email.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Specify the subject of the email.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/MESSAGE'.Message (MESSAGE) - Help
:XH3.MESSAGE - Message
:P.Specifies a message to include in the email, and its content type.
:P.This option is only displayed if the ACTION is *EMAIL.
:H3.Single values
:PARML.
:PT.:PK def.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.This parameter does not place a message in the email.
:EPARML.
:H3.Element 1: Content
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Specify the content placed in the email. CHAR(5000)
:EPARML.
:H3.Element 2: Send as
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.*TEXTPLAIN:EPV.
:PD.Copy the content into the body of the mail message
specifying content type text/plain.
:P.Line breaks can be added by placing hex value X'0D25'
or &CR in the data.
:PT.:PV.*TEXTHTML:EPV.
:PD.Copy the content into the body of the mail message
specifying content type text/html.
:P.Line breaks can be added by placing &CR or '<br>' in the
data.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/OBJ'.Objects (OBJ) - Help
:XH3.OBJ - Objects
:P.Specifies the path name of additional objects to send. A maximum
of 64 path names can be specified. The object must already exist in
the IFS.
:P.This option is only displayed if the ACTION is *EMAIL.
:H3.Single values
:PARML.
:PT.:PK def.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.No objects are sent.
:EPARML.
:H3.Element 1: Name
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Specify an object path name. CHAR(128)
:EPARML.
:H3.Element 2: Send as
:PARML.
:PT.:PK def.*ATTACH:EPK.
:PD.Send the object as an attached file using MIME and
specifying "application/octet-stream". This works for
most PC type files.
:PT.:PV.*TEXTPLAIN:EPV.
:PD.Copy the object into the body of the mail message
specifying content type text/plain. The CCSID of the
file must match the value specified for CHRENC().
:NT.Some servers disregard this request and
form an attachment from the message in all cases.
Some servers disregard this request for the second
and subsequent body parts. If this is the case,
try MSG(*NONE).:ENT.
:PT.:PV.*TEXTHTML:EPV.
:PD.Copy the object into the body of the mail message
specifying content type text/html. The CCSID of the
file must match the value specified for CHRENC().
:NT.Some servers disregard this request and
form an attachment from the message in all cases.
Some servers disregard this request for the second
and subsequent body parts. If this is the case,
try MSG(*NONE).:ENT.
:PT.:PV.*ATTACHPDF:EPV.
:PD.Send the object as an attached file using MIME and
specifying "application/pdf". Use this value if the
attached file contains Adobe's Portable Document
Format (pdf) data.
:PT.:PV.*ATTACHPS:EPV.
:PD.Send the object as an attached file using MIME and
specifying "application/postscript". Use this value if
the attached file contains postscript data.
:PT.:PV.*NOTE:EPV.
:PD.Same as *TEXTPLAIN which is preferred.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/INCVARS'.Include Variable Overrides (INCVARS) - Help
:XH3.INCVARS - Incldue Varialbe Overrides
:P.Specifies wether or not to include the values of the variable
overrides in the body of the email.
:P.This option is only displayed if the ACTION is *EMAIL.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK def.*NO:EPK.
:PD.Variable Overrides are not included in the body of the email.
:PT.:PV.*YES:EPV.
:PD.Varaible overrides are included in the body of the email. The
message text will be displayed first then a list of all variables
and the values they are overridden to are appended to the end of
the email body.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/PFILE'.Physical File (PFILE) - Help
:XH3.PFILE - Physical File
:P.Specifies name of a physical file to create and place the output
into. The file cannot exist or the program will produce an error.
:P.This option is only displayed if the ACTION is *OUTFILE.
:H3.Element 1: Output File
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Enter the name of the file to be created. CHAR(10)
:EPARML.
:H3.Element 2: Library
:PARML.
:PT.:PK def.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job is used.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Enter the library name to create the file in. CHAR(10)
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/IFSFOLDER'.Folder Name (IFSFOLDER)- Help
:XH3.IFSFOLDER - Folder Name
:P.Specifies the name of the folder the output file will be placed in.
The name is a path and should start with /.
:P.This option is only displayed if the ACTION is *IFSFILE.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/IFSFILE'.File Name (IFSFILE)- Help
:XH3.IFSFILE - File Name
:P.Specifies the name of the file created. Do not include
the file extension, it will be added automatically based on the file
type parameter.
:P.This option is only displayed if the ACTION is *IFSFILE.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/IFSTYPE'.File Type (IFSTYPE)- Help
:XH3.IFSTYPE - File Type
:P.Specifies the type of file to contain the queries output.
The valid type are:
:UL.
:LI.:HP2.*XLS:EHP2. - Creates an Excel file.
:LI.:HP2.*XML:EHP2. - Creates an Excel formatted XML file.
:LI.:HP2.*CSV:EHP2. - Creates a Comma Separated Variable text file.
:EUL.
:P.This option is only displayed if the ACTION is *IFSFILE.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/OUTQ'.Output Queue (OUTQ)- Help
:XH3.OUTQ - Output Queue
:P.Specifies the output queue to place the printed output into.
:H3.Single values
:PARML.
:PT.:PK def.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The output will be placed in the output queue from the
current job definition.
:EPARML.
:H3.Element 1: Output Queue
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Specify the output queue to place the output in.
:EPARML.
:H3.Element 2: Library
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.Library:EPV.
:PD.Enter the library name of the output queue, if
left blank *LIBL will be used.
:EPARML.
:P.This option is only displayed if the ACTION is *PRINT.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/TITLE'.Report Title (TITTLE)- Help
:XH3.TITLE - Report Title
:P.Specifies the title to use at the top of the report. The value of
*DFT will use the name of a saved query definition. If the query is
being passed to the command the there will not be a title unless it
is entered here.
:P.This option is only displayed if the ACTION is *PRINT.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/COPIES'.Copies (COPIES)- Help
:XH3.COPIES - Copies
:P.Specifies the number of copies to print.  Defaults to 1, cannot
be greater than 255.
:P.This option is only displayed if the ACTION is *PRINT.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/HOLD'.Hold Output (HOLD)- Help
:XH3.HOLD - Hold Output
:P.Specifies whether to hold the output in the output queue.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK def.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The output is not put on hold.
:PT.:PV.*YES:EPV.
:PD.The output is put on hold.
:EPARML.
:P.This option is only displayed if the ACTION is *PRINT.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/SAVE'.Save Output (SAVE)- Help
:XH3.SAVE - Save Output
:P.Specifies whether to save the output after it has printed.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK def.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The output is not saved.
:PT.:PV.*YES:EPV.
:PD.The output is saved.
:EPARML.
:P.This option is only displayed if the ACTION is *PRINT.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/USRDTA'.User Datat (USRDTA)- Help
:XH3.USRDTA - User Data
:P.Specifies the user data for spool file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK def.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The user data will contain the query name.
:PT.:PV.character value:EPV.
:PD.Enter a value to be used for the user data. Char(10)
:EPARML.
:P.This option is only displayed if the ACTION is *PRINT.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/WIDTH'.Width (WIDTH)- Help
:XH3.WIDTH - Width
:P.Specifies the width of the spool file. The default is 132.
Any data that does not fit in the width is trunctated. The width
also determines the CPI. See the chart below for details.
:XMP.
 up to    80  -  CPI(10)  Portrait
 81   -   96  -  CPI(12)  Portrait
 97   -  132  -  CPI(12)  Landscape
 133  -  198  -  CPI(15)  Landscape
 over 198     -  CPI(18)  Landscape
:EXMP.
:P.This option is only displayed if the ACTION is *PRINT.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/LENGTH'.Length (LENGTH)- Help
:XH3.LENGTH - Length
:P.Specifies the page length of the spool file. The default is 66.
:P.This option is only displayed if the ACTION is *PRINT.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/PINVR'.Include variables (PINVR)- Help
:XH3.PINVR - Include Variables
:P.Designates whether variable values are included on the report or
not. If a Y is entered in this parameter, the first page of the report
will include any variable values before the detail starts to print.
:P.The varaibles have to defined in a saved query deffinition or
nothing will be included. If varaiable overrides are passed to the
command then the values passed will be included. Otherwise the query
will be run with the default values and they will be listed.
:P.This option is only displayed if the ACTION is *PRINT.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/PINQY'.Include Query (PINQY)- Help
:XH3.PINQY - Include Querys
:P.Designates whether to print the passed query or not. If a Y is
entered in this parameter, the report will include a paritially
formatted printout of the SQL statement passed to the print program.
:P.The formatting is simple because the query statment is passed as
a compressed string. This means any formatting done in a saved query
definition is stipped and not included in this printout.
:P.This option is only displayed if the ACTION is *PRINT.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/PNAME'.Program Name (PNAME)- Help
:XH3.PNAME - Program Name
:P.Allows entry of a program name. The name is used wheN creating
a printed report or a PDF file. It is used In the headings to simulate
standard report formatting. The name is optional and will not be
included if it is not passed.
:P.The name should be passed if a program is creating a report. The
name should be the name of the RPG or CL program creating the report.
:P.This option is only displayed if the ACTION is *PRINT or if a PDF
file is being created. If creating an Excel or CSV file
use the sheet name
to show the program name, include it in on a title line or incoprerate
it into the file name, subject or email message.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQL/VAROVR'.Variable overrides (VAROVR) - Help
:XH3.VAROVR - Variable overrides
:P.Specifies values to use for specific variables. The entry requires a
variable name and a value. The variables are setup in the query
definition and the names must match. Each variable setup is also
given a type. The value entered for the variable name must match
the type the varaible is defined for.
:P.This option is only displayed if the ACTION is *PRINT,
*EMAIL, *DISPLAY, *OUTFILE OR *IFSFILE.
:H3.Element 1: Variable
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Enter the name of the variable to override. CHAR(10)
:EPARML.
:H3.Element 2: Value
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Enter the value to override the variable to. CHAR(30)
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQLF1'.Query Manager - List Screen
:XH3.Screen 1 - List Screen
:P.This screen is the primary maintenance screen. It lists
the queries that have already been setup. From this screen queries can
maintained or added.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQLF1F'.
:XH3.Command Keys
:P.This screen has the following command keys:
:P.:HP2.F1=Help:EHP2. Displays this help text.
:P.:HP2.F3=Exit:EHP2. Exits the program.
:P.:HP2.F4=Ad Hoc:EHP2. Open the ad hoc query screen.
:P.:HP2.F6=Add:EHP2. Opens a screen to create a new query.
:P.:HP2.F8=Sort Toggle:EHP2. Toggles the sort between entry date and
query description.
:P.:HP2.F9=User/Date Toggle:EHP2. Toggles the user and date between
entry and last revised values.
:P.:HP2.F11=Show Deleted Toggle:EHP2. Toggles between showing and hiding
deleted entries.
:P.:HP2.F12=Cancel:EHP2. Cancels any options and returns to the previous
screen.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQLF1/USER'.User
:XH3.USER - User
:P.This option restricts the queries in the list to a spceific user. The
system is setup to allow different user to create queries with the same
name. This means that each user has thier own list of queries. However
each user can work witrh another users queries by enter that users profile
name in the field. If the fiels is left blank the list will include all
queries setup in the system.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQLF1/SRCH'.Search Field
:XH3.SEARCH - Search Field
:P.The search field allows limiting the data in the list. The field
handles multiple words and returns any lines that have the search
criteria.
:P.For example if "TEST PROGRAM" is entered in the search field an
entry with the text of "TESTING THIS PROGRAM" would show up because
it contains both character sets from the search string.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQLF1/SELECT'.Selection Column
:XH3.SELECT - Selection Column
:P.This column allows selecting a specific entry to preform an action
to.
The screen alwo allows IBM's standard options although they are not
listed in the options. They are included in the list below.
The options are listed above the list in blue.
:H2.Options
:UL.
:LI.:HP2.X/2:EHP2.=Update, Allows maintenance on the query.
:LI.:HP2.V/5:EHP2.=View, Displays the queries definition.
:LI.:HP2.R/1:EHP2.=Run, Brings up a screen to run the query.
:LI.:HP2.C/3:EHP2.=Copy, Copys an entry to a new one.
:LI.:HP2.D/4:EHP2.=Delete, Deletes an entry.
:LI.:HP2.E/7:EHP2.=Reinstate, Reinstates a deleted entry.
Only shown if deleted entries are displayed.
:LI.:HP2.A/9:EHP2.=Open in Ad Hoc, copies the query into the ad hoc screen
:EUL.
:P.Enter an option in the selection column next to the query that you
want to perform that action to. The program will automatically perform
the option, there is no need to press enter.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQLF1/SF1NAME'.Name Column
:XH3.Name Column
:P.This column shows the name of the query.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQLF1/SF1type'.Type Column
:XH3.Type Column
:P.This column shows the type of the query.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQLF1/SF1desc'.Description Column
:XH3.Description Column
:P.This column shows the queries description.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQLF1/SF1LRUS'.User Column
:XH3.User Column
:P.This column shows the entry or the last change user. Use F9 to
toggle which value is shown
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQLF1/SF1LRDT'.Date Column
:XH3.Date Column
:P.This column shows entry date or the last change date. Use F9 to
toggle which value is shown
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQLF2'.Query Manager - View Screen
:XH3.Screen 2 - View Screen
:P.This screen displays all properties of a save query.
:XH3.Command Keys
:P.This screen has the following command keys:
:P.:HP2.F1=Help:EHP2. Displays this help text.
:P.:HP2.F3=Exit:EHP2. Exits the program.
:P.:HP2.F12=Cancel:EHP2. Cancels any options and returns to the previous
screen.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQLF3'.Query Manager - Add/Maintenance Screen
:XH3.Screen 3 - Add/Maintenance Screen
:P.This screen allows changing header level information about the query.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQLF3F'.
:XH3.Command Keys
:P.This screen has the following command keys:
:P.:HP2.F1=Help:EHP2. Displays this help text.
:P.:HP2.F3=Exit:EHP2. Exits the program.
:P.:HP2.F12=Cancel:EHP2. Cancels any options and returns to the previous
screen.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQLF3/F3NAME'.Query Name
:XH3.Query Name
:P.The query name is a unqique name that is used to run and select
the query.
:P.The name must be unique for an individual user. The name can exist
under multiple user though. The name cannot begin with #$LST because
these special names are used to save the last run queries for each
user.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQLF3/F3DESC'.Query Description
:XH3.Query Description
:P.The query description is a breife description of what the query is
used for. This is the description that is displayed on the search
screen. It is also the field used when entering a search parameter.
:P.The decription should be something meaningful that describes what
the query produces. It should also include the terms that would be
used when searching for this query in the future.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQLF3/F3TYPE'.Query Type
:XH3.Query Type
:P.The query type is required however it is for reference only. As of
now the progrma onyl works with select queries so that is the only
value that should be entered in the type.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQLF3/F3OUTP'.Default Output Type
:XH3.Default Output Type
:P.The default output type is used when a user runs the query. The
type can be overidden at run time so just enter the prefered run type
here. The values are lsited below:
:UL.
:LI.:HP2.1:EHP2.=Display
:LI.:HP2.2:EHP2.=Print
:LI.:HP2.3:EHP2.=Email
:EUL.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQLF3/F3EM01'.Default Email Address
:XH3.Default Email Address
:P.The default email address is used when the query is run using the
SQL command. It is only used if an email address of *DFT is entered
on the command.
:P.If an email address is entered here it must be valid or an error
will be displayed.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQLF3/F3VROV'.Enter Variables
:XH3.Enter Variables
:P.This option allows variable to be entered for the SQL statement.
These variable can be overriden at run time.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQLF3/F3LD01'.Long Description/Notes
:XH3.Long Description/Notes
:P.The long description is just that, a lond description. It can be
used to document the query or just as notes. It is not required, so
you can leave it blank if you want.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SQLF3/F3ENUS'.Entry Information
:XH3.Entry Information
